      bearCase: "Persistent global risk aversion, continued high interest rates in developed markets, and a strengthening US dollar could lead to prolonged FII outflows. This, combined with potential domestic inflation pressures and a widening current account deficit due to high crude oil prices, could significantly weigh on Indian market performance and the Rupee.",
